-- title:
--   Base smooth-point stalks and Drinfeld identification from an affine chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Further data: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places, namely those places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places for level $M'$, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen` lying in the supersingular $j$-set `ssJSet q`; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the field generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $M'$ inside Laurent series) into `fieldBar q M'` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'`); a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants and with orders of places; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which states that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` belongs to $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and has $R_0$-residue equal to the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$; and a distinguished element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   A base field layer is fixed: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, together with the hypotheses that $A \cap k_0$ (formally, the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is Henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and the approximation hypothesis `hκ`: every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Auxiliary arithmetic data: a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Finally a bottom layer: an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (`hAb`), and an element $\varpi_b \ne 0$ of $A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   With $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the assertion is the following implication, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$. The antecedent is the conjunction of nine clauses, named here:
--
--   (K1) the compositum of $F_0$ with the constants, $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\mathrm{range}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M')) \sqcup F_0$, is all of `fieldBar q M'`;
--   (K2) for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$;
--   (K3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring;
--   (K4) the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$;
--   (K5) there is $t \in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, then every coefficient of $p$ maps into $W_0$ and lies in its maximal ideal;
--   (RED) for every $g$ in the full modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and which satisfies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j_q)$, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion `hle` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of this image and $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$;
--   (EQ) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` maps $F_0$ into itself and preserves membership in $W_0$;
--   (LD) for every finite-dimensional intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of } K') \sqcup F_0$: if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, then all $a_i = 0$;
--   (MODEL) there are a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a$ under $K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`; $B$ is contained in $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of } K_b) \sqcup F_0$ and every element of that field is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ away from $\varpi_b$, in the sense that $f \in W_0$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$; the image of $j_q$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $B$; $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and, for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the $C_s$-fixed subfield of the Drinfeld function field) with $\#C_s = 2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, with kernel the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, agreeing on $A_b$ with reduction $A_b \to \kappa$ followed by the structure map, such that every $z$ in the target is of the form $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$, such that the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those $z$ whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), and such that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f \in B$ one has $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}\,f) =$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$, as elements of the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   The consequent repeats the eight clauses (K1), (K2), (K3), (K4), (K5), (RED), (EQ), (LD) verbatim, and replaces (MODEL) by the following clause (STALKS).
--
--   (STALKS) For every field $F_{SS}$ equipped with an algebra structure over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{SS}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with surjective residue map onto $F_{SS}$ of kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants and with the scaling property), such that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f \in W_0$, the conjunction of the following two statements holds.
--
--   First, for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e : F_{SS} \simeq$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with $\#C_s = 2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every hypothesis $h_\tau$ that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every membership $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and every $x \in F_{SS}$, the image under $e$ of $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` applied to $x$ equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $e(x)$, in the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Second, there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$, an assignment $Q \mapsto S_Q$ of subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q : A_b[X] \to S_Q$, ring homomorphisms $\chi_Q : S_Q \to \kappa$, and sets $D_Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, such that:
--
--   $\#N = q+1$;
--
--   there is a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` with $B \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $B \subseteq S_Q$ for every $Q \notin N$, and such that every $z \in F_{SS}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $Q \notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$;
--
--   for every $Q \notin N$: the image of every $a \in A_b$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is that image for every $a \in A_b$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; $S_Q$ is local with $\ker \chi_Q$ its maximal ideal; $S_Q$ is contained in $\mathrm{adjoin}_{k_0}(\text{image of } K_b) \sqcup F_0$ and every element of that field is a quotient of two elements of $S_Q$ with non-zero denominator; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; $S_Q \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$ and an element of $S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if it is divisible by $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$; for every $f \in S_Q$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in the residue field of $Q$ is the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has $Q$-order equal to $1$; and $D_Q$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which are rational, for which every $f \in S_Q$ is $P$-regular with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for which, for every $f \in S_Q$, the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f) = 0$;
--
--   the discs are pairwise disjoint: if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q = Q'$;
--
--   cusp-freeness: for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $j_q$ in `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   and equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every hypothesis that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every place $Q$ of $F_{SS}$: $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$, and if $Q \notin N$ then $\{P : \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D_Q\} = D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q}$.
--
--   This is the passage, at a given pair $(F_0, W_0)$, from an affine chart of the descended semistable model along the supersingular part of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ to the geometric data of the special fibre: the identification of the residue field of a regular prolongation with the $C_s$-invariants of the Drinfeld function field $xy^q - x^qy = 1$ over the residue field of $A$, level-equivariantly, together with the base-layer smooth-point stalks $S_Q$ (étale coordinate $\varphi_Q(X)$, residue character $\chi_Q$, residue disc $D_Q$) at the places off the $q+1$ ends, the discs being disjoint, cusp-free and permuted compatibly with the ends. It feeds the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_affineChart).
